From dd2feeb7ad0fb40eb24b162c94fb39df321338a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:01:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc/examples/Makefile.example: add filter_audio

filter_audio is built by "make examples" in the source tree, but it is
missing from the standalone Makefile that gets installed along with the
example sources. It calls sin(), so it also needs the math library.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/Makefile.example | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/examples/Makefile.example b/doc/examples/Makefile.example
index dee9ebf..422c062 100644
--- a/doc/examples/Makefile.example
+++ b/doc/examples/Makefile.example
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ EXAMPLES=\
                 encode_audio                       \
                 encode_video                       \
                 extract_mvs                        \
+                filter_audio                       \
                 hw_decode                          \
                 mux                                \
                 remux                              \
@@ -43,6 +44,7 @@ OBJS=$(addsuffix .o,$(EXAMPLES))
 # the following examples make explicit use of the math library
 avcodec:           LDLIBS += -lm
 encode_audio:      LDLIBS += -lm
+filter_audio:      LDLIBS += -lm
 mux:               LDLIBS += -lm
 resample_audio:    LDLIBS += -lm
 
-- 
2.43.0

